      "writtenOn": "2026-04-27T16:58:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Missing Error Check on File Length (`fun.c`)** The function `calc_file_len` uses `fseek` and `ftell`, returning an `int`. If `ftell` fails, it returns `-1`. The calling code (`downloadbin` and `VerifyData`) does not check for negative values.\n\n```c\nfile_len \u003d calc_file_len(file); // If this returns -1...\nbuffer \u003d (unsigned char *)malloc(file_len + 16); // malloc(15) due to integer overflow/truncation\ncnt \u003d fread(buffer, 1, file_len, file); // Attempts to read MAX_UINT bytes into a 15-byte buffer.\n```\n\n  **Remediation:** Check `if (file_len \u003c 0)` immediately after returning from `calc_file_len` and exit gracefully.",
