      "writtenOn": "2026-04-27T16:58:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Double Initialization / Resource Leak (`net_usb.c` \u0026 `main.c`)** In `main.c`, `ft_device_init` makes these consecutive calls:  \n    \n  1. `mbedtls_usb_exist(\u0026pid, \u0026vid);`  \n  2. `mbedtls_usb_init(pid, vid);`\n\n\n  Both functions contain this logic: `ret \u003d libusb_init(\u0026usb_ctx-\u003ectx);`. Because `usb_ctx-\u003ectx` is initialized twice without a corresponding `libusb_exit`, the original context is leaked, and the internal state of `libusb` is corrupted. **Remediation:** Refactor context management. Call `libusb_init` exactly once during application startup (or carefully pair each init with an exit).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "224ab4101f31c3c479a37aa3873281064504d008",
