      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Use Standard String Comparisons (`main.c`)** The codebase currently uses `memcmp` to evaluate command-line arguments:\n\n```c\nif (!memcmp(tmp, \"force_update_full_ec_bin\", sizeof(\"force_update_full_ec_bin\")))\n```\n\n  While technically safe here because `tmp` is strictly bounds-checked and `memset` to zero beforehand, it is non-standard and brittle. **Remediation:** Replace these with standard string comparisons like `strncmp(tmp, \"force_update_full_ec_bin\", PATH_MAX) \u003d\u003d 0`.",
