      "writtenOn": "2026-04-27T16:58:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Memory Corruption via Hotplug Callback Pointer (`net_usb.c`)** In `mbedtls_usb_init`, the arguments passed to `libusb_hotplug_register_callback` are misaligned:\n\n```c\nret \u003d libusb_hotplug_register_callback(\n    usb_ctx-\u003ectx, ..., usb_event_callback,\n    \u0026callback_handle, \u0026hp[0]);\n```\n\n  Here, `\u0026callback_handle` is passed as the `user_data` argument, and `\u0026hp[0]` is passed as the handle pointer. Inside `usb_event_callback`, `user_data` is cast to an `int*` and overwritten:\n\n```c\nint *ret \u003d (int *)user_data;\nif (ret) {\n    *ret \u003d 0x55aa;\n}\n```\n\n  This overwrites `callback_handle` with `0x55aa`. Later, `mbedtls_usb_free` tries to deregister the callback using this corrupted handle, which will fail or crash. **Remediation:** Pass a proper flag variable pointer (like `\u0026g_no_device_flag` or a dedicated status variable) for `user_data`, and pass `\u0026callback_handle` as the final argument.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 149,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 60
      },
